EXPERIMENT 6 – LEAP YEAR CHECKING USING JUNIT

AIM
To write JUnit test cases to check whether a given year is a leap year and validate the output using JUnit assertions.

ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the JUnit 5 dependency.
2. Create a class named YearUtil.
3. Write the isLeapYear() method using the leap year condition.
4. Create YearUtilTest with different test cases.
5. Use assertTrue() and assertFalse() to verify results.
6. Run the tests using mvn test.

CODE
YearUtil.java
public class YearUtil {
    public static boolean isLeapYear(int year) {
        return (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0)
                || (year % 400 == 0);
    }
}


YearUtilTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class YearUtilTest {
    @Test
    void yearDivisibleBy4IsLeap() {
        assertTrue(YearUtil.isLeapYear(2024));
    }

    @Test
    void centuryYearIsNotLeap() {
        assertFalse(YearUtil.isLeapYear(1900));
    }

    @Test
    void centuryYearDivisibleBy400IsLeap() {
        assertTrue(YearUtil.isLeapYear(2000));
    }

    @Test
    void ordinaryYearIsNotLeap() {
        assertFalse(YearUtil.isLeapYear(2023));
    }
}


